  "prompt": "Detect every curb ramp in this street-level image. A curb ramp (curb cut) is an intentional sloped transition that lowers a sidewalk curb to street level to provide barrier-free passage to the roadway, typically located at intersections, street corners, or aligned with pedestrian crosswalks. Detect curb ramps even if partially obscured by pedestrians, street vendors, utility poles, or street clutter. Do not detect utility access covers, drainage slabs, stairs, driveways, or tactile paving and concrete patches that sit atop full-height curbs with a vertical drop-off. The ramp must visibly grade down to meet the street surface for pedestrian crossing. Return one tight bounding box per curb ramp. If there are no curb ramps, return an empty list."
